For the exact fixed-capacity effect map \(\vartheta_N\) of Definition \(\mathrm{fitted\mbox{-}center}\),
\[
 \vartheta_N(p;M_N)=\theta_N,
 \qquad
 \sup_{p\in\mathcal P,\,|\gamma|\leq G}
 \left\|\nabla_{p'}\vartheta_N(p';M_N)\big|_{p'=p}-A\right\|\longrightarrow0. \tag{11}
\]
On \([c/2,2C]^3\), for every fixed interior capacity \(M\), the map \(p'\mapsto\vartheta_N(p';M)\) is twice continuously differentiable and
\[
 \sup_{p'\in[c/2,2C]^3,\,1\leq M\leq N-1}
 \|\nabla_{p'}^2\vartheta_N(p';M)\|\leq C_*\sqrt N             \tag{12}
\]
for a finite constant \(C_*\) depending only on \((c,C)\).
